<title>SPAIN: Peseta debt/interbank closing report.</title>
<headline>Peseta debt/interbank closing report.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1996-09-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spanish government bonds corrected in afternoon trade as non-residents took positions ahead of the release of U.S. August payroll data on Friday, dealers said.</p>
<p>Although volume was not significant, non-residents were restocking their portfolios with Spanish and Italian debt in anticipation of a rise in U.S. employment. &quot;They're squaring positions ahead of tomorrow,&quot; said an analyst.</p>
<p>Economists polled by Reuters expect the U.S. unemployment rate to fall to 5.3 percent in August from 5.4 percent in July.</p>
<p>The dollar's rebound, attributed to technical factors, was also expected to help domestic bonds.</p>
</text>
